---
title: Variant files
description: Author tailwind-variants recipes so stories, types, and installs stay in sync.
order: 3
---

Any file named `*.variants.ts` under `registry/items/**` must follow the recipe in [`button.variants.ts`](/components/button). That file is the source of truth. Do not inline `tv({ base, variants })` inside `.svelte` files or hardcode variant-name arrays in stories.

## Layout

Keep the recipe next to the component (kebab-case names matching the item folder):

```text
registry/items/components/button/
  button.svelte
  button.variants.ts
  button.types.ts
  _registry.mdx
  _preview.svelte
```

Multi-part items can add part-scoped recipes such as `item-media.variants.ts` or `empty-media.variants.ts`. Re-export from `index.ts` when the item has a barrel.

## Recipe

Split the variant map from the `tv()` call. Export key lists from `Object.keys` for stories and docs previews:

```ts
import { tv } from 'tailwind-variants';

export const exampleCva = {
	variants: {
		variant: {
			default: 'bg-primary text-primary-foreground',
			outline: 'border-border bg-background'
		},
		size: {
			default: 'h-9 px-4 text-sm',
			sm: 'h-8 px-3 text-xs'
		}
	},
	defaultVariants: {
		variant: 'default',
		size: 'default'
	}
} as const;

export const exampleVariants = tv({
	base: 'inline-flex items-center rounded-md font-medium disabled:opacity-50',
	...exampleCva
});

export const EXAMPLE_VARIANTS = Object.keys(
	exampleCva.variants.variant
) as (keyof typeof exampleCva.variants.variant)[];

export const EXAMPLE_SIZES = Object.keys(
	exampleCva.variants.size
) as (keyof typeof exampleCva.variants.size)[];
```

Export one `Object.keys` list per **string** axis that stories or docs need (`variant`, `size`, `tone`, and so on). Skip boolean axes.

Simpler single-axis recipes (for example `alert.variants.ts`) may call `tv({ base, variants, defaultVariants })` directly and export `VariantProps` types from the same file.

If the file defines more than one recipe, repeat the same config → `tv` → keys sequence for each.

## Types and usage

Put `VariantProps` aliases in `<name>.types.ts` when that file exists. Derive them from the `tv` export, not from a duplicated string union:

```ts
import type { VariantProps } from 'tailwind-variants';
import { exampleVariants } from './example.variants';

export type ExampleVariant = VariantProps<typeof exampleVariants>['variant'];
export type ExampleSize = VariantProps<typeof exampleVariants>['size'];
```

In the Svelte component, compose classes with `cn` from `$lib/utils.js`:

```svelte
<script lang="ts" module>
	import { cn } from '$lib/utils.js';
	import type { ExampleProps } from './example.types';
	import { exampleVariants } from './example.variants';
</script>

<script lang="ts">
	let {
		class: className,
		variant = 'default',
		size = 'default',
		...restProps
	}: ExampleProps = $props();
</script>

<div class={cn(exampleVariants({ variant, size }), className)} {...restProps}></div>
```

Re-export the recipe from `index.ts` when present:

```ts
export {
	exampleVariants,
	exampleCva,
	EXAMPLE_VARIANTS,
	EXAMPLE_SIZES
} from './example.variants.js';
```

Stories and `_preview.svelte` should import those key lists for options instead of repeating names by hand.

## Checklist

- Use only `tv` from `tailwind-variants` (see `button.variants.ts`). Do not use `class-variance-authority` / `cva`.
- Use kebab-case file names (`button.variants.ts`, not `Button.variants.ts`).
- Name the helpers `{name}Cva`, `{name}Variants`, and `{NAME}_VARIANTS` / `{NAME}_SIZES` when exporting key lists.
- Derive published key lists from `Object.keys(config.variants.*)`.
- Derive prop types from `VariantProps<typeof …Variants>`, not hand-written unions.
- List the `.variants.ts` file in `_registry.mdx` `files` when the item publishes it.
